# A Noughts and crosses game, written down move by move.
#
# Lines that are not comments are commands, exactly as they are typed at the
# prompt. Undo and redo are moves like any other, so reading this file back
# retraces the game as it was really played - second thoughts and all - and
# arrives at the same position it was saved from.
#
#   dotnet run -- tictactoe replay <this file>

deal 2 639221025526283931

#   1  turn 1, X
place 5
#      X takes square 5.

#   2  turn 2, O
place 1
#      O takes square 1.

#   3  turn 3, X
place 2
#      X takes square 2.

#   4  turn 4, O
place 3
#      O takes square 3.

#   5  turn 5, X
place 4
#      X takes square 4.

#   6  turn 6, O
place 6
#      O takes square 6.

#   7  turn 7, X
place 7
#      X takes square 7.

#   8  turn 8, O
place 8
#      O takes square 8.

#   9  turn 9, X
place 9
#      X takes square 9.
#      The game is over: the board is full and neither has three in a row.
